.TH COWRITER 1 "October 2026" "Co-Writer 4.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cowriter, cowriter-gui \- local research and writing workspace
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cowriter-gui
.RI [ FILE ...]
.br
.B cowriter
.RI [ FILE ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Co-Writer opens a native GTK desktop editor with document tabs, Markdown preview,
a notebook, offline spelling and common grammar checks, and poetry tools.
Both commands launch the same application.
Local file arguments open as document tabs in the existing application window.
.PP
The optional Poetry & prose window provides rhythm and rhyme hints, personal
reading marks, repetition exploration, reference examples, and private notes.
These tools run locally without an AI model or network service.
Reading marks and craft notes are stored separately from manuscript text.
.PP
The optional assistant connects to Ollama for local AI tasks.
Evidence searches contact the selected scholarly services.
Desktop sharing creates copies for external applications, and the Open Pressroom
handoff transfers an article copy with its linked evidence reports.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --help
Show application options and exit.
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B Ctrl+N, Ctrl+O, Ctrl+S
Create, open, or save a document.
.TP
.B F7
Visit the next spelling or grammar issue.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Alt+P
Open Poetry & prose tools.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+P
Open Markdown preview.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/cowriter/
Local preferences, workspace, recovery copies, and versions.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/cowriter/proofreading-words.json
Personal spelling dictionary.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/cowriter/poetry-notes/
Private craft annotations associated with each document path.
.SH SEE ALSO
Installed README and packaging guide in
.IR /usr/share/doc/cowriter/ .
